++# [Informational] Studio Configuration Reference
++
++Authoritative technical reference specification for all configuration attributes, execution tiers, and administrative controls across all 11 👍kanban Studios.
++
++---
++
++## 1. Workspace Studio (`#workspace-studio`)
++
++The Workspace Studio (`/workspaces/:ws/settings` or `/admin/workspaces`) manages top-level tenancy, membership defaults, data lifecycle policies, and security guardrails.
++
++<a id="workspace-configuration"></a>
++<a id="workspace-studio"></a>
++
++### Workspace Studio Configuration Table
++
++| Field Name | What It Controls | Allowed Values / Format | Default | Security / Operational Impact |
++| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
++| `name` | Human-readable name of the workspace displayed in header and navigation | UTF-8 String (1 to 128 characters) | Required at provisioning | Public within workspace; visible to all members and invited guests |
++| `slug` | URL-safe workspace identifier used in API routes and web paths | Lowercase alphanumeric ASCII with hyphens (2 to 64 chars) | Derived from name | Immutable after creation; binds database RLS tenancy context |
++| `default_role` | Default permission tier assigned to newly provisioned local users | `WORKSPACE_MEMBER`, `WORKSPACE_VIEWER`, `WORKSPACE_GUEST` | `WORKSPACE_MEMBER` | Restricts baseline capabilities before explicit project assignments |
++| `trash_retention_days` | Number of days soft-deleted items remain in Trash Studio before automated purge | Integer between 7 and 365 | 30 | Governs compliance data retention; automated purge requires daemon runner |
++| `auto_archive_threshold_days` | Inactivity duration after which closed tickets are automatically archived | Integer between 0 and 730 (0 disables auto-archive) | 90 | Keeps active board queries lightweight; archived tickets remain search-indexable |
++| `max_projects_limit` | Maximum number of active projects allowed within this workspace | Positive integer (1 to 1000) | 50 | Resource cap preventing tenant sprawl and memory exhaustion |
++| `air_gap_enforced` | Strict zero-egress flag blocking all external cloud AI and runner connections | Boolean (`true` / `false`) | `false` | When enabled, only local Ollama models and internal runners execute |
++| `allowed_email_domains` | Comma-separated domain allowlist for user registration and invite cards | List of valid domain strings (e.g. `corp.example.com`) | Empty (Allow all verified) | Rejects non-corporate email addresses at registration gate |
++
++---
++
++## 2. Project Studio (`#project-studio`)
++
++The Project Studio (`/projects/:proj/settings`) configures project-level attributes, work item defaults, view presets, and planning dimensions.
++
++<a id="project-configuration"></a>
++<a id="project-studio"></a>
++
++### Project Studio Configuration Table
++
++| Field Name | What It Controls | Allowed Values / Format | Default | Security / Operational Impact |
++| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
++| `name` | Display name of the project | UTF-8 String (1 to 128 characters) | Required at creation | Scoped to workspace; surfaced in command palette and breadcrumbs |
++| `key` | Prefix key for issue identifiers (e.g. `KAN-142`) | Uppercase ASCII alphanumeric (2 to 10 characters) | Required at creation | Immutable; generates human-readable issue keys across all surfaces |
++| `description` | Markdown overview and charter for the project | Canonical UTF-8 Markdown (up to 10,000 characters) | Empty | Sanitized server-side; safe Mermaid and media proxying enabled |
++| `default_workflow_id` | Identifier of active workflow managing state transitions | Valid UUID of existing project workflow | Default Kanban Workflow | Determines active transition gates, validators, and AI agent checks |
++| `auto_archive_days` | Project-specific threshold for archiving closed work items | Integer (0 to 365, 0 = inherit workspace) | 0 | Overrides workspace retention for high-velocity software teams |
++| `enable_cycles` | Toggles Agile/Scrum cycle and sprint planning features | Boolean (`true` / `false`) | `true` | Enables cycle velocity tracking, start/end dates, and rollover |
++| `enable_modules` | Toggles functional module breakdown and progress roll-ups | Boolean (`true` / `false`) | `true` | Allows hierarchical grouping of work items under functional deliverables |
++| `wip_limits_enforcement` | Behavior when Kanban column WIP limits are exceeded | `warn`, `strict_block`, `disabled` | `warn` | `strict_block` rejects card drop operations exceeding column capacity |
++| `default_assignee_mode` | Initial assignment policy for newly authored work items | `unassigned`, `project_lead`, `creator` | `unassigned` | Prevents orphaned tickets and automates triage assignment |
++
++---
++
++## 3. Workflow Transition Studio (`#workflow-studio`)
++
++The Workflow Transition Studio (`/projects/:proj/settings/workflows`) defines state groups, transition helper hooks, synchronous validators, and asynchronous AI agent gates.
++
++<a id="workflow-configuration"></a>
++<a id="workflow-studio"></a>
++
++### Workflow Transition Studio Configuration Table
++
++| Field Name | What It Controls | Allowed Values / Format | Default | Security / Operational Impact |
++| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
++| `state_name` | Human-readable label for the workflow state | String (1 to 64 characters) | Required (e.g. `In Review`) | Appears on board columns, peek drawers, and transition selectors |
++| `state_group` | Standardized category mapping for cycle metrics | `backlog`, `unstarted`, `started`, `completed`, `cancelled` | `started` | Used in velocity burn-down and sub-issue progress roll-ups |
++| `helper_type` | Engine used to evaluate transition eligibility | `wasm_validator`, `wasm_mutator`, `agent_gate` | `wasm_validator` | Governs execution latency and synchronous vs asynchronous processing |
++| `hook_path` | Target module, wasm bytecode, or agent identifier | File path, slug, or registered agent UUID | Required | Executes within sandboxed environment with strict resource caps |
++| `failure_policy` | Action taken if transition helper rejects or times out | `BLOCK_TRANSITION`, `WARN_AND_ALLOW`, `PROVISIONAL_HOLD` | `BLOCK_TRANSITION` | Fail-closed invariant preventing invalid transitions into protected states |
++| `execution_timeout_ms` | Maximum allowed wall-clock execution time | 50ms to 30000ms (Sync Wasm: <=250ms) | 100ms | Prevents hanging transitions and thread pool starvation |
++| `sandbox_tier` | Isolation level enforced during helper execution | `wasm` (in-process wasmtime) or `nsjail` (container) | `wasm` | Sandboxed with zero network or filesystem syscall access |
++
++---
++
++## 4. Custom Fields Studio (`#custom-fields-studio`)
++
++The Custom Fields Studio (`/projects/:proj/settings/custom-fields`) defines dynamic metadata, computed story points, and sandboxed formulas.
++
++<a id="custom-fields-configuration"></a>
++<a id="custom-fields-studio"></a>
++
++### Custom Fields Studio Configuration Table
++
++| Field Name | What It Controls | Allowed Values / Format | Default | Security / Operational Impact |
++| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
++| `name` | Human-readable label displayed on ticket rails and tables | String (1 to 64 characters) | Required | Displayed alongside execution status badge (`🧪`) |
++| `slug` | Unique field identifier used in formulas and JSON payloads | Lowercase alphanumeric ASCII with hyphens | Derived from name | Used in formula expressions and API JSON properties |
++| `flavor` | Execution tier and computation engine | `scalar`, `formula`, `wasm`, `nsjail` | `formula` | Determines performance budget and standalone mode availability |
++| `sandbox_tier` | Multi-tier sandbox engine used for execution | `scalar`, `wasmtime` (Tier A), `nsjail` (Tier B) | `wasmtime` | `nsjail` requires multi-container compose; fail-closed in standalone |
++| `credential_mode` | Token identity provided during script execution | `INVOKING_USER`, `SERVICE_ACCOUNT` | `INVOKING_USER` | `SERVICE_ACCOUNT` requires dual-control cryptographic approval |
++| `target_scope` | Maximum tenant visibility boundary of the field | `PROJECT`, `WORKSPACE`, `SERVER` | `PROJECT` | Escalation beyond `PROJECT` requires AAL2 administrative step-up |
++| `output_format` | Canonical schema used to format and render output | `text`, `number`, `badge`, `severity_pill`, `url`, `markdown_snippet`, `json_table` | `text` | Enforces strict Pydantic validation before persisting to JSONB |
++| `format_metadata` | Configuration options tailored to chosen output format | JSON object matching schema specification | `{}` | Governs decimal precision, color tokens, allowlists, or table headers |
++| `script_source` | Raw source code for formula or script evaluation | Python AST expression, Rust Wasm, or container script | Required | Signed with SHA-256 digest upon commit; immutable against database tampering |
++| `egress_allowlist` | Allowed destination hostnames for nsjail tier | Comma-separated domain list (e.g. `api.github.com`) | Empty (Zero egress) | Network disabled by default via Linux kernel `CLONE_NEWNET` |
++
++---
++
++## 5. Authentication Studio (`#auth-studio`)
++
++The Multi-Card Authentication Studio (`/admin/auth`) configures enterprise identity providers, WebAuthn Passkeys, LDAP trees, and break-glass recovery.
++
++<a id="authentication-configuration"></a>
++<a id="auth-studio"></a>
++
++### Authentication Studio Configuration Table
++
++| Field Name | What It Controls | Allowed Values / Format | Default | Security / Operational Impact |
++| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
++| `provider_type` | Underlying identity protocol card | `LOCAL_ADMIN`, `OAUTH2`, `OIDC`, `LDAP`, `WEBAUTHN`, `TOTP` | Required | Determines credential validation handshake and token exchange |
++| `card_enabled` | Master active toggle for the authentication card | Boolean (`true` / `false`) | `true` | Disabled cards reject authentication attempts immediately |
++| `sort_rank` | Order in which login cards appear on `/login` screen | Non-negative integer (lower ranks appear first) | 10 | Allows organizations to prioritize SSO while preserving local admin cards |
++| `rp_name` | WebAuthn Relying Party display name | String (Always canonical `👍kanban`) | `👍kanban` | Displayed by browser and hardware security keys during passkey prompts |
++| `rp_id` | WebAuthn Relying Party domain identifier | Strict ASCII FQDN without protocol or port | Hostname of deployment | Must match browser origin to prevent credential theft or spoofing |
++| `issuer_url` | OIDC discovery endpoint URL | Valid HTTPS URL | None | Fetches `/.well-known/openid-configuration` and cryptographic keys |
++| `client_id` | OAuth/OIDC application client identifier | ASCII string | None | Public identifier registered with enterprise identity provider |
++| `client_secret` | OAuth/OIDC client secret credential | Encrypted string (write-only custody) | None | Stored encrypted in PostgreSQL; never exposed over REST API |
++| `ldap_host` | LDAPS directory hostname or IP address | Hostname or IP | None | LDAPS on port 636 or StartTLS required; plaintext LDAP rejected |
++| `ldap_bind_dn` | Distinguished Name used for directory lookup | LDAP DN string (e.g. `cn=admin,dc=corp,dc=com`) | None | Service account with read-only search permissions across user tree |
++| `break_glass_active` | Emergency lockout prevention bypass trigger | Boolean (`true` / `false`) | `false` | Allows emergency local admin access when SSO is offline |
++
++---
++
++## 6. MCP Access Studio (`#mcp-studio`)
++
++The MCP Access Studio (`/settings/mcp` or `/admin/mcp`) manages Model Context Protocol API tokens, Level of Detail (LOD) defaults, and rate limits.
++
++<a id="mcp-configuration"></a>
++<a id="mcp-studio"></a>
++
++### MCP Access Studio Configuration Table
++
++| Field Name | What It Controls | Allowed Values / Format | Default | Security / Operational Impact |
++| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
++| `surface_type` | Target isolated streamable endpoint | `/mcp/agent`, `/mcp/docs`, `/mcp/admin` | `/mcp/agent` | Determines tool catalog and token budget ceiling (<= 1,850 tokens for agent) |
++| `key_name` | Descriptive name of the API token or client tool | String (1 to 64 characters) | Required | Surfaced in audit logs and active session inspector |
++| `token_prefix` | Standardized key prefix identifying privilege level | `kb_agt_*`, `kb_doc_*`, `kb_adm_*` | Auto-assigned | Cryptographically identifies target surface before database lookup |
++| `lod_tier` | Default Level of Detail returned in tool responses | `summary`, `standard`, `full` | `standard` | Controls response verbosity; `summary` minimizes agent context consumption |
++| `rate_limit_rpm` | Maximum allowed tool invocations per minute | Integer between 10 and 600 | 120 | Protects database connection pool from runaway autonomous agent loops |
++| `expires_at` | Expiration timestamp for the API key | ISO-8601 Timestamp or `None` | 90 days from creation | Expired keys reject calls with `401 UNAUTHORIZED` |
++| `destructive_gate` | Enables two-stage confirmation for destructive operations | Boolean (`true` / `false`) | `true` | Requires short-lived confirmation token before permanent deletions |
++
++---
++
++## 7. OAuth 2.1 Governance Studio (`#oauth-studio`)
++
++The OAuth 2.1 Governance Studio (`/admin/oauth`) registers client applications, enforces PKCE code challenges, and configures token lifetimes.
++
++<a id="oauth-configuration"></a>
++<a id="oauth-studio"></a>
++
++### OAuth 2.1 Governance Studio Configuration Table
++
++| Field Name | What It Controls | Allowed Values / Format | Default | Security / Operational Impact |
++| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
++| `client_name` | Name of the integrating client application | String (1 to 128 characters) | Required | Displayed on user authorization consent screens |
++| `client_id` | Unique OAuth client identifier | String prefixed with `kb_client_` | Auto-generated | Public application key used during authorization code flow |
++| `redirect_uris` | Allowed callback URLs for authorization codes | List of strict HTTPS URLs (localhost allowed for dev) | Required | Exact string matching enforced; wildcards strictly forbidden |
++| `pkce_enforced` | Proof Key for Code Exchange requirement | Mandatory `S256` challenge | `S256` | Rejects plaintext code challenges; mitigates authorization code interception |
++| `allowed_scopes` | List of privilege scopes client can request | `agent`, `docs`, `admin`, `read:issues`, `write:issues` | `agent` | Token capability bitmask cannot exceed granted scopes |
++| `access_token_ttl` | Lifetime of minted access tokens | Integer seconds (300 to 86400) | 3600 (1 hour) | Ephemeral lifetime limiting blast radius of token leakage |
++| `refresh_token_ttl` | Lifetime of rotating refresh tokens | Integer seconds (86400 to 2592000) | 2592000 (30 days) | Refresh tokens rotate upon use; reused tokens revoke family |
++
++---
++
++## 8. AI Providers Studio (`#ai-studio`)
++
++The AI Providers Studio (`/admin/ai`) registers model providers, configures write-only API keys, and sets monthly token consumption caps.
++
++<a id="ai-configuration"></a>
++<a id="ai-studio"></a>
++
++### AI Providers Studio Configuration Table
++
++| Field Name | What It Controls | Allowed Values / Format | Default | Security / Operational Impact |
++| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
++| `provider_key` | Underlying AI provider implementation | `openai`, `gemini`, `ollama`, `custom` | `gemini` | Selects prompt serializer, tool calling dialect, and streaming pipeline |
++| `priority` | Fallback dispatch order when multiple providers are active | Integer (1 to 100, higher runs first) | 10 | Primary provider attempted first; falls back on rate limit or 5xx |
++| `api_endpoint` | Base URL for API communications | Valid HTTP/HTTPS URL | Official cloud endpoint | Local Ollama uses `http://localhost:11434`; cloud requires HTTPS |
++| `api_key` | Cryptographic API secret for provider access | String (Write-only custody) | None | Stored encrypted in PostgreSQL; never sent back to browser client |
++| `monthly_token_cap` | Monthly token consumption budget ceiling | Non-negative integer (0 = unlimited) | 1,000,000 | Blocks cloud invocations once budget is reached to prevent cost overruns |
++| `default_model` | Model identifier used for sparkle and transition gates | String (e.g. `gemini-2.5-flash`, `gpt-4o`) | Provider default | Balances reasoning capability against response latency |
++| `temperature` | Randomness parameter for model generations | Float between 0.0 and 1.0 | 0.2 | Low temperatures ensure deterministic responses for code and QA gates |
++
++---
++
++## 9. Agent Definitions Studio (`#agents-studio`)
++
++The Agent Definitions Studio (`/admin/agents`) authors system personas, binds autonomous agents to service accounts, and configures execution harnesses.
++
++<a id="agents-configuration"></a>
++<a id="agents-studio"></a>
++
++### Agent Definitions Studio Configuration Table
++
++| Field Name | What It Controls | Allowed Values / Format | Default | Security / Operational Impact |
++| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
++| `agent_name` | Unique name and identifier for the autonomous agent | String (1 to 64 characters) | Required | Used in ticket mentions, activity streams, and assignment cards |
++| `system_prompt` | Core instructions, persona guidelines, and security boundaries | UTF-8 Markdown text | Required | Directs model reasoning; stripped of dangerous injection sequences |
++| `execution_harness` | Runtime environment executing agent invocations | `api_direct`, `cli_pipe`, `remote_runner` | `api_direct` | `cli_pipe` uses zero-shell `agy -p` or `codex -p` in Linux jail |
++| `cli_pipe_binary` | Binary path used for zero-shell CLI pipe harness | Pre-approved binary name (`agy`, `codex`) | `agy` | Executes without shell or bash; communicates strictly over STDIN/STDOUT |
++| `service_principal_id` | Bound service account identity for database RLS | Valid UUID of service principal | Auto-provisioned | Binds database permissions to caller identity via `SET LOCAL` |
++| `repository_access` | Git repository access mode granted to the agent | `none`, `ro_mount`, `ephemeral_clone` | `none` | `ro_mount` mounts repository strictly read-only for forensic QA |
++
