-    "content": "# Real-Time Web and WebSocket Architecture\n\n## Overview\n\nModern software engineering teams collaborate concurrently across distributed locations. When one developer moves a card on the Kanban board, adds a comment, or when an autonomous AI agent updates a verification gate, all team members viewing the project must see the update instantly without manual page refreshes.\n\n\ud83d\udc4dkanban implements a high-performance **Real-Time WebSocket Hub** (`kanban/realtime/hub.py` and `kanban/api/ws.py`) delivering sub-50ms event fan-out across browser clients and autonomous agents.\n\n---\n\n## WebSocket Hub Architecture\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    subgraph Clients[\"Subscribed Clients\"]\n        Browser[\"Browser Clients (Chrome / Firefox / Safari)\"]\n        Agents[\"Autonomous Agents & IDE Integrations\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Gateway[\"WebSocket Ingress (/ws/v1)\"]\n        Ingress[\"FastAPI WebSocket Handler<br/>- Origin header CORS check<br/>- Session cookie / Bearer token resolution<br/>- 16-connection limit per principal\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Router[\"Realtime Hub Event Router\"]\n        Hub[\"Hub Event Router (kanban/realtime/hub.py)<br/>- Channels: workspace:{id}, project:{id}, issue:{id}<br/>- RLS permission-filtered fanout<br/>- Non-blocking async backpressure queues\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Surfaces[\"Live UI Surfaces\"]\n        BoardUI[\"Board View: Instant Card Moves (<12ms)\"]\n        DrawerUI[\"Ticket Drawer: Live Activity & Gate Timers\"]\n        StickyUI[\"Stickies Grid: Collaborative Autosave\"]\n    end\n\n    Browser --> Ingress\n    Agents --> Ingress\n    Ingress --> Hub\n    Hub --> BoardUI\n    Hub --> DrawerUI\n    Hub --> StickyUI\n```\n\n![Responsive Tablet and Mobile Layout with Live Realtime Updates](images/30-responsive-tablet-layout.png)\n\n---\n\n## Connection Security and Rate-Limiting Controls\n\nWebSockets establish persistent, bidirectional TCP connections that can be abused for denial-of-service (DoS) or unauthorized event eavesdropping if not hardened properly.\n\n### 1. Strict Origin and CSRF Validation\nDuring the initial WebSocket upgrade handshake (`GET /ws/v1`), the server validates the incoming `Origin` header against configured allowed hosts. Requests from untrusted origins are immediately rejected with HTTP 403 Forbidden.\n\n### 2. Session Authentication and Privilege Resolution\n- WebSocket connections authenticate using encrypted session cookies (`__Host-kb_session`) or scoped Bearer API tokens.\n- Anonymous WebSocket connections are strictly forbidden.\n- When an authenticated connection opens, the hub resolves the user's principal ID, active tenant workspace, and project memberships.\n\n### 3. Maximum 16 Concurrent Connections per Principal\nTo prevent browser tab flooding or malicious connection exhaustion:\n- The `ConnectionManager` tracks open sockets by `principal_id`.\n- If an individual user or service principal attempts to establish more than 16 concurrent WebSocket connections, excess connection requests are rejected with status code `4429 Too Many Connections`.\n\n---\n\n## Channel Subscription and Event Model\n\nClients subscribe to targeted channels based on their active view, minimizing unnecessary network traffic:\n\n| Channel Pattern | Granularity | Typical Subscribers | Broadcast Events |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **`workspace:{workspace_id}`** | Workspace | All active workspace members | Project creation, system announcements, sticky note grid updates. |\n| **`project:{project_id}`** | Project | Users viewing board or issue list | `ISSUE_MOVED`, `ISSUE_CREATED`, `CYCLE_ACTIVATED`, `MODULE_UPDATED`. |\n| **`issue:{issue_id}`** | Ticket | Users viewing Ticket Peek Drawer | `COMMENT_ADDED`, `GATE_STATUS_CHANGED`, `ASSIGNEE_UPDATED`. |\n\n### Core Broadcast Events\n\n- **`ISSUE_MOVED`:** Dispatched when a card changes state or swimlane position. Transmits the updated state ID, previous state ID, sort rank, and the operator who initiated the move.\n- **`GATE_STATUS_CHANGED`:** Broadcasts async agent gate transitions (`pending_agent_gate`, `vetoed`, `approved`) allowing the board to update countdown timers and animate spring snap-backs in real time.\n- **`STICKY_UPDATED`:** Broadcasts real-time color changes, text edits, or promotion events on the stickies masonry grid.\n\n---\n\n## Client Resilience and Reconnection Strategy\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    autonumber\n    actor User as Connected Operator\n    participant Client as React 19 WebSocket Client\n    participant Hub as Realtime Hub\n    participant DB as PostgreSQL Ledger\n\n    Note over Client,Hub: Normal Operation (Receiving Events)\n    Hub->>Client: Event: ISSUE_MOVED (seq: 42)\n    Note over Client,Hub: Network Partition / Laptop Lid Closed\n    Client->>Client: Connection Lost! Activate Reconnecting Pill\n    Note over Client,Hub: Network Restored\n    Client->>Hub: Reconnect Handshake & Resume (last_seq: 42)\n    Hub->>DB: Query Activity Ledger WHERE seq > 42\n    DB-->>Hub: Return Events [seq: 43, 44, 45]\n    Hub-->>Client: Replay Catch-Up Events [43, 44, 45]\n    Client->>Client: Update State Store & Set Status Pill to Connected\n```\n\nNetwork connections in modern development environments (laptops switching networks, sleep states, VPN renegotiation) are inherently unstable.\n\nThe \ud83d\udc4dkanban web client implements robust reconnection resilience:\n- **Exponential Backoff with Jitter:** On connection loss, the client attempts reconnection starting at 500ms, doubling up to a maximum 10-second cap with random jitter to prevent connection storms.\n- **Event Sequence Numbers:** Every event payload includes a monotonically increasing `seq` integer. On reconnect, the client requests missed events since its last acknowledged sequence number, guaranteeing zero missed updates.\n- **Visual Connection Pill:** A discrete indicator in the UI status bar displays real-time WebSocket connectivity (`Connected`, `Reconnecting`, `Offline`).\n\n![Async Agent Gate States with Live Realtime Timers](images/16-async-agent-gate-states.png)\n"
+    "content": "# [Architectural] Real-Time Web and WebSocket Architecture\n\n## Overview\n\nModern software engineering teams collaborate concurrently across distributed locations. When one developer moves a card on the Kanban board, adds a comment, or when an autonomous AI agent updates a verification gate, all team members viewing the project must see the update instantly without manual page refreshes.\n\n\ud83d\udc4dkanban implements a high-performance **Real-Time WebSocket Hub** (`kanban/realtime/hub.py` and `kanban/api/ws.py`) delivering sub-50ms event fan-out across browser clients and autonomous agents.\n\n---\n\n## WebSocket Hub Architecture\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    subgraph Clients[\"Subscribed Clients\"]\n        Browser[\"Browser Clients (Chrome / Firefox / Safari)\"]\n        Agents[\"Autonomous Agents & IDE Integrations\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Gateway[\"WebSocket Ingress (/ws/v1)\"]\n        Ingress[\"FastAPI WebSocket Handler<br/>- Origin header CORS check<br/>- Session cookie / Bearer token resolution<br/>- 16-connection limit per principal\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Router[\"Realtime Hub Event Router\"]\n        Hub[\"Hub Event Router (kanban/realtime/hub.py)<br/>- Channels: workspace:{id}, project:{id}, issue:{id}<br/>- RLS permission-filtered fanout<br/>- Non-blocking async backpressure queues\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Surfaces[\"Live UI Surfaces\"]\n        BoardUI[\"Board View: Instant Card Moves (<12ms)\"]\n        DrawerUI[\"Ticket Drawer: Live Activity & Gate Timers\"]\n        StickyUI[\"Stickies Grid: Collaborative Autosave\"]\n    end\n\n    Browser --> Ingress\n    Agents --> Ingress\n    Ingress --> Hub\n    Hub --> BoardUI\n    Hub --> DrawerUI\n    Hub --> StickyUI\n```\n\n![Responsive Tablet and Mobile Layout with Live Realtime Updates](images/30-responsive-tablet-layout.png)\n\n---\n\n## Connection Security and Rate-Limiting Controls\n\nWebSockets establish persistent, bidirectional TCP connections that can be abused for denial-of-service (DoS) or unauthorized event eavesdropping if not hardened properly.\n\n### 1. Strict Origin and CSRF Validation\nDuring the initial WebSocket upgrade handshake (`GET /ws/v1`), the server validates the incoming `Origin` header against configured allowed hosts. Requests from untrusted origins are immediately rejected with HTTP 403 Forbidden.\n\n### 2. Session Authentication and Privilege Resolution\n- WebSocket connections authenticate using encrypted session cookies (`__Host-kb_session`) or scoped Bearer API tokens.\n- Anonymous WebSocket connections are strictly forbidden.\n- When an authenticated connection opens, the hub resolves the user's principal ID, active tenant workspace, and project memberships.\n\n### 3. Maximum 16 Concurrent Connections per Principal\nTo prevent browser tab flooding or malicious connection exhaustion:\n- The `ConnectionManager` tracks open sockets by `principal_id`.\n- If an individual user or service principal attempts to establish more than 16 concurrent WebSocket connections, excess connection requests are rejected with status code `4429 Too Many Connections`.\n\n---\n\n## Channel Subscription and Event Model\n\nClients subscribe to targeted channels based on their active view, minimizing unnecessary network traffic:\n\n| Channel Pattern | Granularity | Typical Subscribers | Broadcast Events |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **`workspace:{workspace_id}`** | Workspace | All active workspace members | Project creation, system announcements, sticky note grid updates. |\n| **`project:{project_id}`** | Project | Users viewing board or issue list | `ISSUE_MOVED`, `ISSUE_CREATED`, `CYCLE_ACTIVATED`, `MODULE_UPDATED`. |\n| **`issue:{issue_id}`** | Ticket | Users viewing Ticket Peek Drawer | `COMMENT_ADDED`, `GATE_STATUS_CHANGED`, `ASSIGNEE_UPDATED`. |\n\n### Core Broadcast Events\n\n- **`ISSUE_MOVED`:** Dispatched when a card changes state or swimlane position. Transmits the updated state ID, previous state ID, sort rank, and the operator who initiated the move.\n- **`GATE_STATUS_CHANGED`:** Broadcasts async agent gate transitions (`pending_agent_gate`, `vetoed`, `approved`) allowing the board to update countdown timers and animate spring snap-backs in real time.\n- **`STICKY_UPDATED`:** Broadcasts real-time color changes, text edits, or promotion events on the stickies masonry grid.\n\n---\n\n## Client Resilience and Reconnection Strategy\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    autonumber\n    actor User as Connected Operator\n    participant Client as React 19 WebSocket Client\n    participant Hub as Realtime Hub\n    participant DB as PostgreSQL Ledger\n\n    Note over Client,Hub: Normal Operation (Receiving Events)\n    Hub->>Client: Event: ISSUE_MOVED (seq: 42)\n    Note over Client,Hub: Network Partition / Laptop Lid Closed\n    Client->>Client: Connection Lost! Activate Reconnecting Pill\n    Note over Client,Hub: Network Restored\n    Client->>Hub: Reconnect Handshake & Resume (last_seq: 42)\n    Hub->>DB: Query Activity Ledger WHERE seq > 42\n    DB-->>Hub: Return Events [seq: 43, 44, 45]\n    Hub-->>Client: Replay Catch-Up Events [43, 44, 45]\n    Client->>Client: Update State Store & Set Status Pill to Connected\n```\n\nNetwork connections in modern development environments (laptops switching networks, sleep states, VPN renegotiation) are inherently unstable.\n\nThe \ud83d\udc4dkanban web client implements robust reconnection resilience:\n- **Exponential Backoff with Jitter:** On connection loss, the client attempts reconnection starting at 500ms, doubling up to a maximum 10-second cap with random jitter to prevent connection storms.\n- **Event Sequence Numbers:** Every event payload includes a monotonically increasing `seq` integer. On reconnect, the client requests missed events since its last acknowledged sequence number, guaranteeing zero missed updates.\n- **Visual Connection Pill:** A discrete indicator in the UI status bar displays real-time WebSocket connectivity (`Connected`, `Reconnecting`, `Offline`).\n\n![Async Agent Gate States with Live Realtime Timers](images/16-async-agent-gate-states.png)\n"
   },
